# Conditionals: `@if`, `@else if`, and `@else` 🔀

Conditionally include styles based on configuration flags, themes, or argument values.

```scss_not
@mixin theme-banner($theme: 'light') {
  padding: 24px;
  border-radius: 8px;

  @if $theme == 'light' {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    color: #0f172a;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  } @else if $theme == 'dark' {
    background-color: #0f172a;
    color: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid #334155;
  } @else if $theme == 'cyberpunk' {
    background-color: #0d0221;
    color: #00f0ff;
    border: 1px solid #ff007f;
  } @else {
    @error "Invalid theme '#{$theme}' passed to theme-banner mixin!";
  }
}
```

# The `@each` Loop with Lists 📋

The `@each` rule evaluates a block of styles for each item in a list.

```scss_not
$social-networks: facebook, twitter, linkedin, github, youtube;

@each $network in $social-networks {
  .icon-#{$network} {
    background-image: url('/icons/#{$network}.svg');
    background-size: cover;
  }
}
```

## Compiles To:
```css_not
.icon-facebook { background-image: url('/icons/facebook.svg'); background-size: cover; }
.icon-twitter { background-image: url('/icons/twitter.svg'); background-size: cover; }
.icon-linkedin { background-image: url('/icons/linkedin.svg'); background-size: cover; }
.icon-github { background-image: url('/icons/github.svg'); background-size: cover; }
.icon-youtube { background-image: url('/icons/youtube.svg'); background-size: cover; }
```

# The `@each` Loop with Maps 🗺️

Iterating over key-value maps is how design systems like Bootstrap generate hundreds of color utility classes.

```scss_not
$theme-colors: (
  'primary': #4f46e5,
  'success': #10b981,
  'warning': #f59e0b,
  'danger':  #ef4444,
  'dark':    #0f172a
);

// Iterate with two variables: $key and $value
@each $name, $hex in $theme-colors {
  // Background utilities
  .bg-#{$name} {
    background-color: $hex !important;
  }

  // Text color utilities
  .text-#{$name} {
    color: $hex !important;
  }
}
```

> ⚡ **Instant Productivity:** 10 lines of Sass generate 10 complete background and text color utility classes!

# The `@for` Loop: `through` vs `to` 🔢

The `@for` directive loops over a consecutive sequence of numbers.

## 1. `@for $var from <start> through <end>` (Inclusive)
Loops up to AND including the end value:

```scss_not
// Loops 1, 2, 3, 4
@for $i from 1 through 4 {
  .col-#{$i} {
    width: $i * 25%;
  }
}
```

## 2. `@for $var from <start> to <end>` (Exclusive)
Loops up to BUT NOT INCLUDING the end value:

```scss_not
// Loops 1, 2, 3 (STOPS before 4!)
@for $i from 1 to 4 {
  .order-#{$i} { order: $i; }
}
```

> ⚠️ **Rule of Thumb:** In 99% of layout tasks, use `through` so the final index is included!

# Building a 12-Column Grid System with `@for` 📐

Let's generate a full 12-column responsive grid layout using `@for` and `math.div`:

```scss_not
@use 'sass:math';

.row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-left: -12px;
  margin-right: -12px;
}

@for $i from 1 through 12 {
  .col-#{$i} {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    flex: 0 0 math.div($i, 12) * 100%;
    max-width: math.div($i, 12) * 100%;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
  }
}
```

This effortlessly generates `.col-1` (8.333%), `.col-2` (16.666%) up to `.col-12` (100%).

# The `@while` Loop 🔄

The `@while` directive repeats its block until its conditional statement evaluates to `false`.

```scss_not
// Generate exponential spacing utilities (8px, 16px, 32px, 64px, 128px)
$step: 1;
$size: 8px;

@while $size <= 128px {
  .p-#{$step} {
    padding: $size;
  }

  $size: $size * 2; // Double the size
  $step: $step + 1;
}
```

> ⚠️ **Infinite Loop Warning:** Always ensure your `@while` condition increments/mutates towards termination, or the compiler will hang indefinitely!

# Compiler Diagnostics: The `@error` Directive 🛑

The `@error` directive stops compilation immediately and prints a fatal error message with a full stack trace.

```scss_not
@mixin z-index($layer) {
  $valid-layers: ('base': 1, 'dropdown': 100, 'modal': 500, 'toast': 1000);

  @if map-has-key($valid-layers, $layer) {
    z-index: map-get($valid-layers, $layer);
  } @else {
    @error "Invalid z-index layer '#{$layer}'! Allowed layers: #{map-keys($valid-layers)}.";
  }
}

.popup {
  // @include z-index('floating'); // FATAL ERROR: Compilation halts with clear message!
}
```

# Compiler Diagnostics: `@warn` & `@debug` ⚠️🐞

## 1. The `@warn` Directive
Prints a warning to the console but allows compilation to continue. Essential for deprecation notices:

```scss_not
@mixin rounded-corners {
  @warn "rounded-corners is deprecated. Please use modern border-radius utilities instead.";
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```

## 2. The `@debug` Directive
Prints variable values and data structures during development to inspect their types:

```scss_not
$colors: ('primary': #4f46e5, 'secondary': #64748b);
@debug $colors; // Prints: DEBUG: (primary: #4f46e5, secondary: #64748b)
```

# Advanced `@each`: Multi-Dimensional Unpacking 🧬

You can iterate over lists of sublists, unpacking multiple variables in each iteration:

```scss_not
// Format: (icon-name, glyph, color)
$icons: (
  ('check',   '\2713', #10b981),
  ('cross',   '\2717', #ef4444),
  ('star',    '\2605', #f59e0b)
);

@each $name, $glyph, $color in $icons {
  .icon-#{$name}::before {
    content: $glyph;
    color: $color;
    margin-right: 6px;
  }
}
```

# Generating CSS Variables via Loops 🎨

Bridge Sass tokens into dynamic browser CSS variables at runtime:

```scss_not
$tokens: (
  'brand': #6366f1,
  'surface': #0f172a,
  'text': #f8fafc,
  'spacing-sm': 8px,
  'spacing-md': 16px,
  'spacing-lg': 32px
);

:root {
  @each $name, $value in $tokens {
    --app-#{$name}: #{$value};
  }
}
```

This outputs clean `:root { --app-brand: #6366f1; ... }` custom properties accessible in client JavaScript!

# Masterwork: Responsive Utility Generator 📱💻

Nest `@each` inside `@each` to generate responsive breakpoint utilities like Tailwind or Bootstrap:

```scss_not
$displays: block, inline-block, flex, inline-flex, none;
$breakpoints: (
  'sm': 640px,
  'md': 768px,
  'lg': 1024px
);

// 1. Base display utilities (d-flex, d-none)
@each $d in $displays {
  .d-#{$d} { display: $d !important; }
}

// 2. Responsive display utilities (d-md-flex, d-lg-none)
@each $bp, $width in $breakpoints {
  @media (min-width: $width) {
    @each $d in $displays {
      .d-#{$bp}-#{$d} { display: $d !important; }
    }
  }
}
```

# Stacking System Automation 📚

Eliminate random `z-index: 999999` bugs across your engineering team:

```scss_not
$z-layers: (base, header, drawer, modal, toast, tooltip);

@for $i from 1 through length($z-layers) {
  $layer-name: nth($z-layers, $i);
  .z-#{$layer-name} {
    z-index: $i * 100;
  }
}
```

Produces `.z-base { z-index: 100; }`, `.z-header { z-index: 200; }`, up to `.z-tooltip { z-index: 600; }`.

# Production Code: Complete Spacing Engine 📐

Here is how a real framework generates margin and padding utilities:

```scss_not
$spacing-steps: (
  0: 0,
  1: 0.25rem,
  2: 0.5rem,
  3: 1rem,
  4: 1.5rem,
  5: 3rem
);

$directions: (
  't': 'top',
  'b': 'bottom',
  'l': 'left',
  'r': 'right'
);

@each $prop, $prefix in ('padding': 'p', 'margin': 'm') {
  @each $step, $val in $spacing-steps {
    // All sides: .p-3, .m-4
    .#{$prefix}-#{$step} { #{$prop}: $val !important; }

    // Directional sides: .pt-3, .mb-2
    @each $dir-code, $dir-name in $directions {
      .#{$prefix}#{$dir-code}-#{$step} { #{$prop}-#{$dir-name}: $val !important; }
    }
  }
}
```

# Inspecting Loop Execution with `@debug` 🔍

When a loop isn't producing the expected CSS output, insert `@debug` to print state directly in your terminal during `sass --watch`:

```scss_not
@each $name, $val in $theme-colors {
  @debug "Generating utilities for color: #{$name}, value: #{$val}";
  .bg-#{$name} { background-color: $val; }
}
```
